    "result_text": "I added the summary panel, and all 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass.\n\n**What changed** (front end only; the server and stored data didn't need to change):\n- **New `features/summary/summary.ts`:** a small panel with three tables (by grade, by period, by status) carrying the `summary-*` test ids the spec expects.\n- **`features/people/people.ts`:** shows the panel and works out its figures from the same values the list already shows, so they always agree with it:\n  - **Per grade (A, B, C):** the people whose grade is that one today, leaving out retired people. Their due-totals are added up the same way as the sheet's due total, so a person showing \"n/a\" adds nothing.\n  - **Per period:** the same due-total the period list shows, including the figure a closed period was fixed at.\n  - **Per status:** how many claims have each of DRAFT, OPEN, PENDING, SETTLED and VOID. The app has no PENDING status, so that count is always 0; it's shown because the spec checks for it.\n\n**Two judgement calls on the rules:**\n- **Retired people's claims still count in the status figures.** The first test needs this: Cam is retired, but Cam's settled and voided claims are in the counts.\n- **Retired means \"has a retire date\", even one after today.** That matches how the list labels and hides retired people. The other reading of \"on that grade today\" would still count someone due to retire later. The tests don't cover that case, so tell me if you want it the other way.",
